+# BLUE CURRENT V46.40.0 — DISPOSABLE RETIREMENT REHEARSAL
+
+## Release scope
+
+V46.36–V46.40 adds the final non-destructive rehearsal layer before any future authoritative code removal.
+
+A proposed retirement is applied only to an isolated temporary repository copy.
+
+### V46.36 — Disposable Repository Copy
+
+The rehearsal service creates an isolated temporary copy of the Blue Current repository.
+
+The authoritative repository is never used as the mutation target.
+
+The temporary copy retains the files needed by the validator, including database migrations and a copied runtime fixture database.
+
+### V46.37 — Simulated Dependency Removal
+
+Inside the disposable copy only, the rehearsal can:
+- remove the candidate HTML section
+- remove candidate script registrations
+- remove candidate module files
+- remove the candidate startup-registry registration
+- remove dependency references from other startup registrations
+- remove known operator rationalization/navigation references
+
+The authoritative source remains untouched.
+
+### V46.38 — Real Rollback Archive + Proposed Change Set
+
+Every rehearsal creates an actual temporary rollback archive in Blue Current rollback JSON format.
+
+The archive contains:
+- exact source file paths
+- SHA-256 hash per backed-up file
+- base64 file content
+- archive scope digest
+
+The rehearsal also generates a proposed simulated change-set artifact.
+
+These artifacts are generated in the temporary rehearsal workspace and are not applied to the authoritative repository.
+
+### V46.39 — Disposable Full Validation
+
+The rehearsal runs the real repository validator on the disposable modified copy.
+
+It also performs a startup syntax check.
+
+Readiness is blocked if:
+- validation fails
+- startup dependencies remain
+- candidate-related API usage remains
+- operational/non-test inbound references remain
+
+Documentation and test references are reported but do not themselves prevent a rehearsal from proving runtime removal safety.
+
+### V46.40 — Authoritative Integrity Certification
+
+Before and after every rehearsal, Blue Current computes a SHA-256 digest over the authoritative source tree.
+
+A successful rehearsal requires identical:
+- source-tree SHA-256
+- source-file count
+
+The resulting safety state remains:
+
+- `authoritativeMutation: false`
+- `authoritativeSafe: true`
+- `codeDeletionAllowed: false`
+- `deletionExecuted: false`
+- `deleteEndpointPresent: false`
+- `tempCopyUsed: true`
+
+A successful rehearsal can reach:
+
+`final-change-set-ready-for-human-review`
+
+This is still not deletion permission.
+
+## New API
+
+- `POST /api/operator-fine-comb/retirement-rehearsal`
+
+The endpoint:
+- requires authentication
+- requires admin permission
+- operates only on an isolated temporary repository copy
+- provides no authoritative delete operation
+
+## UI
+
+Adds the Disposable Retirement Rehearsal center with:
+- human-authorized deletion-plan selector
+- rehearsal trigger
+- simulated change count
+- rollback file count
+- validation result
+- readiness score
+- artifact summary
+- post-removal dependency status
+- explicit no-delete safety checks
+
+## Real Blue Current rehearsal
+
+The focused validation rehearsed retirement of:
+
+`enterpriseValuePlanCenter`
+
+Before simulation:
+- 3 owned files
+- 1 startup-registry dependency
+- 0 proximate API references after scan refinement
+
+After simulated removal:
+- 0 owned files
+- 0 startup-registry dependencies
+- 0 API references
+- remaining references limited to documentation/tests
+
+The disposable copy passed the full validator.
+
+Generated rehearsal artifacts:
+- 7-file rollback archive
+- rollback SHA-256 scope digest
+- 7 simulated changes
+- proposed change set
+
+The authoritative source-tree SHA-256 remained identical before and after.
+
+## Validation
+
+- `node scripts/maintenance/test-retirement-rehearsal.js` passed.
+- Real `enterpriseValuePlanCenter` retirement rehearsal passed in a disposable copy.
+- Startup dependency reduced from 1 to 0 in the simulated copy.
+- Disposable full validation passed.
+- Rollback archive generation passed.
+- Proposed change-set generation passed.
+- Authoritative source-tree digest remained unchanged.
+- `codeDeletionAllowed` remained false.
+- `deletionExecuted` remained false.
+- delete endpoint remained absent.
+- `npm run check` passed:
+  - 834 JavaScript files
+  - 714 client scripts
+  - 5,326 unique HTML IDs
+- Server startup passed as V46.40.0.
+- `/api/health` returned HTTP 200 with database connected and authentication enabled.
+- Authoritative runtime database SHA-256 remained unchanged.
+
+## Fine-comb policy
+
+`simulate-on-disposable-copy-before-any-authoritative-change`
+
+## Next milestone
+
+The next wave should create the final **retirement authorization packet**:
+- bind the human-authorized deletion plan
+- bind the successful rehearsal result
+- bind the rollback digest
+- bind the exact proposed change-set digest
+- require a fresh second human authorization
+- define a short authorization expiry
+- produce a pre-deletion repository tag/checkpoint instruction
+- still stop immediately before authoritative deletion
+
+Only after that explicit gate should Blue Current be considered ready for the first deliberate permanent code retirement.
